One internal package under a command, carrying four directives over declarations the
analysis holds live, so a run measures the withholding a mark cannot do.

Narrowed is referenced only from the file that declares it, so the narrowing kind
reports it and the directive above it withholds that finding. Shared is referenced
from the command's own package, so no narrowing reports it and nothing withholds the
directive naming the same code. The tag parameter of tagged is read nowhere, so the
unused-parameter kind reports a part of a declaration the analysis keeps, and the
directive above the declaration withholds that finding through it. Rowless carries a
directive naming the stale-suppression code, which is a finding about a row of a
document that no record binds to, so that directive withholds nothing and is reported
under the very code it names.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27.1
-- internal/store/store.go --
package store

//deadset:ignore DS1101 -- exported for a reader of this package alone
func Narrowed() int { return 3 }

// Entry is what the command calls, and its body holds the only reference to
// Narrowed and the only call of tagged.
func Entry() int { return Narrowed() + tagged(1, "a") }

//deadset:ignore DS1101 -- the command reaches this one from its own package
func Shared() int { return 2 }

//deadset:ignore DS1801 -- the tag answers a shape this program does not read
func tagged(value int, tag string) int { return value }

//deadset:ignore DS1703 -- a finding about a row of a document has no suppression
func Rowless() int { return 4 }
-- main.go --
package main

import "example.com/app/internal/store"

func main() {
	println(store.Entry(), store.Shared(), store.Rowless())
}
